{"name":"Bloodthirsty Lips","hex":"#c6101e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bloodthirsty","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Thirsty for blood: inexorably violent or eager for bloodshed; murderous.","Of a book, film, etc.: depicting much violence; gory, violent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bloodthirsty"},{"term":"lips","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of lip"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of lip"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lips"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bloodthirsty","blocks":[{"text":"Bloodthirsty is a 1970s Japanese vampire film trilogy produced by Toho Studio, consisting of three of their 1970s horror films: The Vampire Doll, Lake of Dracula and Evil of Dracula. While there is no plot connection between the films, they share a vampire theme. The films were all directed by Michio Yamamoto and co-written by Ei Ogawa."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bloodthirsty","wikidata":"Q11625942"},{"title":"Lip","blocks":[{"text":"The lips are a horizontal pair of soft appendages attached to the jaws and are the most visible part of the mouth of many animals, including humans. Mammal lips are soft, movable and serve to facilitate the ingestion of food and the articulation of sound and speech. Human lips are also a somatosensory organ, and can be an erogenous zone when used in kissing and other acts of intimacy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Lips_2023.jpg/330px-Lips_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lip","wikidata":"Q15173"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/MouthCupidBow.jpg/330px-MouthCupidBow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/MouthCupidBow.jpg/3